desc:Saturator (Magnolius)
// @description Saturator (Magnolius)
// @author Magnolius
// @version 0.1
// @link GitHub https://github.com/m-dahlberg/magnolius-reaper
// @provides
//   gui_kit/gui_kit.jsfx-inc
//   gui_kit/*.png
//   Magnolius_Saturator.help.txt
// @about
//   A saturator with two independent amounts: Symmetric adds odd harmonics,
//   Asymmetric adds even harmonics, so you choose the colour instead of a
//   preset curve. A Slew stage softens fast, loud transients first, the way an
//   op-amp or tape running out of speed does. Knee sets where the odd curve
//   bends. Static auto gain, parallel Mix and 1x/2x/4x oversampling with
//   anti-aliased curves.
//
//   The curves and ideas come from Airwindows (Chris Johnson, MIT licence):
//   Console, Mojo, Spiral, Dyno, Coils and Desk, rebuilt from scratch.
//
//   Latency: 0 / 43 / 46 samples at 1x / 2x / 4x, reported to the host (PDC).
//
//   Licensed GPL-3.0-or-later.
// @changelog
//   First release.

//tags: saturation distortion harmonics tape console colour
// tools/model.py mirrors @init / recalc / @sample sample for sample.  Edit the
// two together; render_test.py's `model` test is what catches a drift.
//
// Signal path, per channel (stereo is unlinked: one shared function, called
// for L and R with its own state):
//
//   x -> Input gain -> upsample (1x: none, 2x, 4x)
//     -> Slew        y += sign(d) sin(min(|d| s R, pi/2)) / (s R),  d = x - y
//     -> Asymmetric  (1-A) x + A (sin(g x + b) - sin b) / (g cos b)
//     -> Symmetric   (1-S) x + S f_k(g x) / g,  f_k(u) = sin(u|u|^k) / |u|^k
//     -> out = dry + HPF_5Hz(stages - dry)     (the residual DC blocker)
//     -> (1-Mix) dry / Input + Mix * autogain * out
//     -> ADAA droop EQ (2x/4x) -> downsample -> Output gain
//
// Stage notes (constants are in @init with their origin):
//   Slew, after Airwindows Desk: saturates the STEP between samples, not the
//     value.  R = OS rate / 48k makes the ceiling a slope per second, so it
//     sounds the same at any rate and oversampling factor.  0 % bypasses it
//     exactly.
//   Asymmetric, after Coils: a biased sine; subtracting sin b removes the
//     static offset and g cos b restores unity small-signal gain.
//   Symmetric + Knee, after Console / Mojo (k = 0.25) / Spiral (k = 1) /
//     Dyno (k = 4).  Knee changes crossfade over 20 ms.
//   Each curve is crossfaded with the dry signal by its own amount, so 0 %
//   is exactly the dry signal.  (The brief's Asymmetric formula alone gives
//   sin(x) at 0 %, which would break the null test.)
//   Each curve flattens at its PEAK: the asymmetric argument is clamped to
//   +-pi/2 and the symmetric u to the peak of f_k (tan v / v = (k+1)/k,
//   v = u|u|^k).  Clamping v at pi/2 instead lets f_k fall again: fold-over.
//   DC: a 5 Hz high-pass on the RESIDUAL (stages minus dry), at the OS rate.
//     It removes the program-dependent offset the Asymmetric stage makes,
//     leaves input DC alone and is bit-exact at neutral, where a high-pass on
//     the whole signal would shift low-frequency phase and fail the null.
//   Auto gain: static.  A table measured by tools/calibrate.py (pink noise,
//     -18 dBFS RMS) over Input x Slew x Asym x Sym for each Knee, read with
//     multilinear interpolation every 32 samples and ramped in between.  The
//     Input gain is divided out exactly, so with no colour the output is the
//     input whatever the Input knob says.
//
// ANTI-ALIASING.  At 2x and 4x both curves run first-order ADAA:
//   y[n] = (F(x[n]) - F(x[n-1])) / (x[n] - x[n-1]),  F' = f,
// falling back to f at the midpoint when the step is tiny.  F is closed form
// for the asymmetric curve and a Hermite table (exact derivatives) for f_k.
// On the linear part ADAA is (1 + z^-1)/2: half an OS sample of delay and a
// cos(w/2) droop per curve.  So the dry signal is "aligned" by exactly the
// same two averages (the residual is then purely the nonlinear part and Mix
// never comb-filters), and a fixed symmetric FIR (tools/design_comp.py)
// undoes cos^2(w/2) to +-0.08 dB at 20 kHz.  ADAA delay + FIR delay is a
// whole number of base samples, so the latency stays an integer.  1x runs
// the plain curves: it is for gentle settings, as the brief says.
//
// OVERSAMPLING: Kaiser halfband FIRs in polyphase form (81 taps, then 21 taps
// for the second 2x of 4x).  Latency = 2*K1 + (ADAA + FIR)/OS, plus K2 at 4x;
// reported through pdc_delay.  Changing the factor resets the oversampler
// (it may click: a setup control).
//
// Every slider label starts with '-', which hides it from REAPER's generic
// slider list (the panel replaces it) while keeping it automatable.
//
// THREADING - do not undo this.  @gfx runs on the UI thread; @init, @slider,
// @block and @sample run on the audio thread.  ALL globals AND all function
// locals and parameters are shared and static.  So:
//   * every @gfx variable and function is g_-prefixed; @gfx loop counters are
//     gi/gj; nothing is named on both sides;
//   * audio thread only: snap_states, rate_params, reset_channels, kn_*,
//     asy_*, hb_*, ag_*, os_sample, os4_pair, ch_proc, the table builders;
//   * @gfx only: every g_* function and every gk_* widget;
//   * the ONE function both threads call is recalc().  It has no parameters,
//     no local() and no loops - every name in it is a global written
//     deterministically from the slider values - so two concurrent calls
//     compute identical results.  It must be callable from @gfx because
//     neither slider_automate() nor sliderchange() re-runs @slider, and
//     @block does not run on a stopped track.  DO NOT ADD locals, parameters
//     or loops to it.
// EEL2 is case-insensitive (asy_C and asy_c are ONE name) and has no
// scientific notation (1e-9 is a silent syntax error that kills the section).
//
// Shared memory, namespaced to this vendor.  ONE slot map for every
// options:gmem=Magnolius plugin:
//   gmem[0]  interface scale, as index+1 (0 = not set yet)
//
// Memory map (words):
//      0..  20  stage-1 halfband taps c[1..K1]
//     32..  37  stage-2 halfband taps c[1..K2]
//     40..  45  ADAA droop EQ taps, 2x      46.. 49  4x
//     64..  95  per-knee scalars (u*, f(u*), F(u*), h, 1/h, k)
//   1024.. 4323 per-knee antiderivative tables: F at +0, f at +520, 1100 each
//   8192..10816 auto-gain table, dB  [knee][input][slew][asym][sym]
//  16384..      channel L: rings up1 +0, up2 +64, dec2 even/odd +128/+192,
//               dec1 even/odd +256/+320, EQ ring +384 (16)
//  17408..      channel R, same layout
//
// Registries:  widget ids 10-15 knobs, 20-23 Knee / Auto Gain buttons,
//              40-42 header controls, 50-55 value fields.
//              string slots 300+ help text.

slider1:input_db=0<-18,18,0.1>-Input (dB)
slider2:slew=0<0,100,0.1>-Slew (%)
slider3:asym=0<0,100,0.1>-Asymmetric (%)
slider4:sym=0<0,100,0.1>-Symmetric (%)
slider5:knee=1<0,2,1{Soft,Medium,Hard}>-Knee
slider6:output_db=0<-18,18,0.1>-Output (dB)
slider7:auto_gain=1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Auto Gain
slider8:mix=100<0,100,0.1>-Mix (%)
slider9:os_i=1<0,2,1{1x,2x,4x}>-Oversampling

options:gmem=Magnolius

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

import gui_kit/gui_kit.jsfx-inc

// Images first and contiguous from 0, the help file LAST.  Never put a
// trailing // comment on these lines: the rest of the line is the path.
filename:0,gui_kit/knob_cyan_grid.png
filename:1,gui_kit/knob_orange_grid.png
filename:2,gui_kit/value_field.png
filename:3,gui_kit/header_bar.png
filename:4,gui_kit/panel_tile.png
filename:5,gui_kit/dropdown.png
filename:6,gui_kit/button_cyan.png
filename:7,gui_kit/button_orange.png
filename:8,gui_kit/bar_cyan_grid.png
filename:9,gui_kit/logo_magnolius_grey.png
filename:10,Magnolius_Saturator.help.txt

@init
gk_init();
gk_img_field = 2; gk_img_header = 3; gk_img_panel = 4;
gk_img_dropdown = 5; gk_img_button = 6;
IMG_COUNT = 10;                 // slots 0..9 are images; 10 is the help file
KNOB_CY = 0; KNOB_OR = 1;
BTN_CY = 6; BTN_OR = 7;
BAR_IMG = 8;
LOGO_IMG = 9;
LOGO_ASPECT = 512/101;

// Grid-packed filmstrips: 8 columns x 8 rows, 64 frames (knobs and the bar).
gk_knob_cols = 8; gk_knob_frames = 64;
gk_bar_cols = 8; gk_bar_frames = 64;

// ---- design size ----
// REAPER opens at the @gfx size, which is a compile-time literal, so keep
// these in step with the "@gfx 720 248" line.  Equivalent sizes: 125 % =
// 900x310, 150 % = 1080x372, 200 % = 1440x496.
UI_W = 720; UI_H = 248;

// ---- interface scale ----
GM_UI_SCALE = 0;
UI_SCALE_DEFAULT = 0;           // 0 = Fit, else an entry in ui_scale()
function ui_scale(idx) ( idx == 1 ? 1 : idx == 2 ? 1.25 : idx == 3 ? 1.5 : idx == 4 ? 2 : 0; );

// ---- help ----
HELP_FILE = 10; HELP_BASE = 300; HELP_MAX = 600;

// ---- constants ----
DB2LOG    = 0.11512925464970229;  // ln(10)/20
HALF_PI   = 1.5707963267948966;
TINY_U    = 10^(-12);             // below this f_k(u) = u.  NOT 1e-12.
SNAP      = 10^(-9);              // a smoothed value this close to its target lands on it
SM_T      = 0.020;                // s, one-pole smoothing of every continuous control (brief)
KNEE_XF_T = 0.020;                // s, Knee crossfade (brief)
SLEW_MAX  = 5;                    // sigma at Slew 100 %.  Tuned by measurement: a
                                  //   0 dBFS 10 kHz sine loses ~14 dB, 1 kHz ~0 dB,
                                  //   -30 dBFS 10 kHz < 0.05 dB
SLEW_REF  = 48000;                // Hz; R = OS rate / SLEW_REF (Desk's home rate)
ASYM_DRIVE = 1;                   // g = 1 + ASYM_DRIVE*A (brief)
B_MAX     = 0.7;                  // rad, bias at Asymmetric 100 % (brief: 0.6..0.8, by ear)
SYM_DRIVE = 2;                    // g = 1 + SYM_DRIVE*S (brief)
DC_HZ     = 5;                    // residual DC blocker corner (brief)
ADAA_EPS  = 0.00001;              // below this |du| ADAA uses f at the midpoint (derived:
                                  //   table error ~1e-14 / 1e-5 stays far below audibility)
FT_N      = 512;                  // antiderivative table intervals per knee
FT_SUB    = 16;                   // Simpson sub-steps per table interval
K1 = 20; BETA1 = 9;               // stage-1 halfband: 4*K1+1 = 81 taps, Kaiser beta
K2 = 5;  BETA2 = 8;               // stage-2 halfband (4x only): 21 taps
AG_BLK    = 32;                   // samples between auto-gain table lookups
AG_NG = 7; AG_NS = 5; AG_NA = 5; AG_NY = 5;   // grid: Input, Slew, Asym, Sym
AG_GMIN = -18; AG_GSTEP = 6;      // Input grid, dB
MTR_FALL_T = 0.300;               // s, meter peak fall (to 1/e)
MTR_RMS_T  = 0.300;               // s, the level-change readout's RMS window
// latency in base samples per oversampling index
LAT1 = 0;
LAT2 = 2*K1 + 3;                  // ADAA 1 + EQ 5 = 6 OS samples = 3
LAT4 = 2*K1 + K2 + 1;             // ADAA 1 + EQ 3 = 4 OS samples = 1

// memory map
C1 = 0; C2 = 32;
COMP2 = 40; COMP4 = 46;
KN_US = 64; KN_FS = 68; KN_FSS = 72; KN_H = 76; KN_IH = 80; KN_K = 84;
KN_TAB = 1024; KN_STRIDE = 1100; KN_FOFF = 520;
AG_TAB = 8192;
CH_L = 16384; CH_R = 17408;
UP1 = 0; UP2 = 64; D2E = 128; D2O = 192; D1E = 256; D1O = 320; EQR = 384;

// ADAA droop compensation (tools/design_comp.py): 1/cos^2(w/2) to 20 kHz.
COMP2[0] = 1.642011249509201;  COMP2[1] = -0.275565674839325;
COMP2[2] = -0.090029061094229; COMP2[3] = 0.034179753494105;
COMP2[4] = 0.030165175766037;  COMP2[5] = -0.019755818081189;
COMP4[0] = 1.629164785203114;  COMP4[1] = -0.275058902597427;
COMP4[2] = -0.083032688526127; COMP4[3] = 0.043509198521997;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- tables

// Kaiser-windowed halfband, 4K+1 taps: the centre tap is 0.5, every other tap
// at an even distance from it is zero, and the K distinct odd-offset taps
// c[1..K] are scaled so the DC gain is exactly 1.
function kaiser_i0(x) local(s, t, k)
(
  s = 1; t = 1; k = 1;
  loop(25, t *= sqr(x*0.5/k); s += t; k += 1;);
  s;
);
function halfband_init(c, kk, beta) local(b0, i, j, w, tot)
(
  b0 = kaiser_i0(beta);
  tot = 0; i = 1;
  loop(kk,
    j = 2*i - 1;
    w = kaiser_i0(beta*sqrt(1 - sqr(j/(2*kk))))/b0;
    c[i] = sin($pi*j*0.5)/($pi*j)*w;
    tot += c[i];
    i += 1;
  );
  i = 1;
  loop(kk, c[i] *= 0.25/tot; i += 1;);
);

// f_k for 0 <= a <= u*.
function kn_fraw(a, kx) local(p)
(
  a < TINY_U ? a : ( p = a^kx; sin(a*p)/p; );
);

// One knee: its peak u* (tan v / v = (k+1)/k, v = u^(k+1)), then f and the
// antiderivative F at FT_N+1 nodes, F by composite Simpson.
function knee_init(kb, kx) local(t, lo, hi, m, v, us, h, hs, fb, ffb, acc, i, j, a)
(
  t = (kx + 1)/kx;
  lo = 0.01; hi = HALF_PI;
  loop(60, m = 0.5*(lo + hi); tan(m)/m < t ? lo = m : hi = m;);
  v = 0.5*(lo + hi);
  us = v^(1/(kx + 1));
  KN_K[kb] = kx;
  KN_US[kb] = us;
  KN_FS[kb] = sin(v)/us^kx;
  h = us/FT_N;
  KN_H[kb] = h;
  KN_IH[kb] = FT_N/us;
  ffb = KN_TAB + kb*KN_STRIDE;
  fb = ffb + KN_FOFF;
  i = 0;
  loop(FT_N + 1, fb[i] = kn_fraw(i*h, kx); i += 1;);
  hs = h/FT_SUB;
  acc = 0; ffb[0] = 0; i = 0;
  loop(FT_N,
    j = 0;
    loop(FT_SUB,
      a = i*h + j*hs;
      acc += hs/6*(kn_fraw(a, kx) + 4*kn_fraw(a + 0.5*hs, kx) + kn_fraw(a + hs, kx));
      j += 1;
    );
    ffb[i + 1] = acc;
    i += 1;
  );
  KN_FSS[kb] = acc;
);

// Auto-gain rows: five Sym values for one (knee, input, slew, asym) cell.
function ag_row(r, v0, v1, v2, v3, v4) local(p)
(
  p = AG_TAB + r*5;
  p[0] = v0; p[1] = v1; p[2] = v2; p[3] = v3; p[4] = v4;
);

// Rate-independent tables, built once per instance.  @serialize is non-empty,
// so REAPER keeps plugin RAM across @init re-runs (transport start, srate).
initdone != 12345 ? (
  initdone = 12345;
  halfband_init(C1, K1, BETA1);
  halfband_init(C2, K2, BETA2);
  knee_init(0, 0.25);             // Soft   - Mojo
  knee_init(1, 1);                // Medium - Spiral
  knee_init(2, 4);                // Hard   - Dyno
  memset(AG_TAB, 0, 3*AG_NG*AG_NS*AG_NA*AG_NY);
// >>> AUTOGAIN TABLE (generated by tools/calibrate.py - do not edit by hand)
  // rows: [knee][input][slew][asym], five Sym values each, dB
  ag_row(0,0.0000,0.0173,0.0177,0.0184,0.0197);
  ag_row(1,0.0176,0.0177,0.0180,0.0188,0.0201);
  ag_row(2,0.0181,0.0182,0.0186,0.0193,0.0206);
  ag_row(3,0.0187,0.0188,0.0191,0.0199,0.0212);
  ag_row(4,0.0187,0.0188,0.0192,0.0199,0.0212);
  ag_row(5,0.0172,0.0173,0.0177,0.0184,0.0197);
  ag_row(6,0.0176,0.0177,0.0180,0.0188,0.0201);
  ag_row(7,0.0181,0.0182,0.0186,0.0193,0.0206);
  ag_row(8,0.0187,0.0188,0.0191,0.0199,0.0212);
  ag_row(9,0.0187,0.0188,0.0192,0.0199,0.0212);
  ag_row(10,0.0173,0.0174,0.0177,0.0185,0.0198);
  ag_row(11,0.0176,0.0177,0.0181,0.0188,0.0201);
  ag_row(12,0.0182,0.0183,0.0186,0.0193,0.0207);
  ag_row(13,0.0187,0.0188,0.0192,0.0199,0.0212);
  ag_row(14,0.0187,0.0189,0.0192,0.0199,0.0213);
  ag_row(15,0.0175,0.0176,0.0179,0.0187,0.0200);
  ag_row(16,0.0178,0.0179,0.0183,0.0190,0.0203);
  ag_row(17,0.0184,0.0185,0.0188,0.0196,0.0209);
  ag_row(18,0.0189,0.0191,0.0194,0.0201,0.0214);
  ag_row(19,0.0190,0.0191,0.0194,0.0202,0.0215);
  ag_row(20,0.0181,0.0182,0.0185,0.0192,0.0206);
  ag_row(21,0.0184,0.0185,0.0188,0.0196,0.0209);
  ag_row(22,0.0189,0.0190,0.0194,0.0201,0.0214);
  ag_row(23,0.0195,0.0196,0.0200,0.0207,0.0220);
  ag_row(24,0.0195,0.0196,0.0200,0.0207,0.0220);
  ag_row(25,0.0000,0.0178,0.0198,0.0239,0.0313);
  ag_row(26,0.0186,0.0193,0.0212,0.0253,0.0327);
  ag_row(27,0.0210,0.0217,0.0236,0.0277,0.0351);
  ag_row(28,0.0240,0.0246,0.0265,0.0307,0.0381);
  ag_row(29,0.0252,0.0258,0.0278,0.0320,0.0395);
  ag_row(30,0.0172,0.0179,0.0198,0.0239,0.0313);
  ag_row(31,0.0187,0.0193,0.0212,0.0253,0.0327);
  ag_row(32,0.0211,0.0217,0.0236,0.0277,0.0351);
  ag_row(33,0.0240,0.0246,0.0266,0.0307,0.0381);
  ag_row(34,0.0252,0.0259,0.0278,0.0320,0.0395);
  ag_row(35,0.0174,0.0181,0.0200,0.0241,0.0315);
  ag_row(36,0.0189,0.0195,0.0214,0.0255,0.0329);
  ag_row(37,0.0213,0.0219,0.0238,0.0279,0.0353);
  ag_row(38,0.0242,0.0248,0.0268,0.0309,0.0383);
  ag_row(39,0.0254,0.0260,0.0280,0.0322,0.0397);
  ag_row(40,0.0183,0.0189,0.0208,0.0249,0.0323);
  ag_row(41,0.0197,0.0203,0.0222,0.0264,0.0337);
  ag_row(42,0.0221,0.0227,0.0246,0.0288,0.0361);
  ag_row(43,0.0250,0.0257,0.0276,0.0317,0.0391);
  ag_row(44,0.0262,0.0269,0.0288,0.0330,0.0405);
  ag_row(45,0.0206,0.0212,0.0231,0.0272,0.0346);
  ag_row(46,0.0220,0.0226,0.0245,0.0286,0.0360);
  ag_row(47,0.0244,0.0250,0.0269,0.0310,0.0384);
  ag_row(48,0.0273,0.0279,0.0299,0.0340,0.0414);
  ag_row(49,0.0285,0.0292,0.0311,0.0353,0.0428);
  ag_row(50,0.0000,0.0207,0.0315,0.0547,0.0959);
  ag_row(51,0.0230,0.0265,0.0373,0.0603,0.1014);
  ag_row(52,0.0331,0.0366,0.0473,0.0703,0.1113);
  ag_row(53,0.0461,0.0496,0.0604,0.0835,0.1247);
  ag_row(54,0.0533,0.0569,0.0684,0.0928,0.1361);
  ag_row(55,0.0173,0.0208,0.0316,0.0547,0.0959);
